WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.438
A closed ticket proves
someone did some work.

2
00:00:02.438 --> 00:00:04.915
An assessed control proves the work held,

3
00:00:04.915 --> 00:00:08.413
and only that belongs in front
of an authorizing official.

4
00:00:08.413 --> 00:00:13.250
The program's rule: if a system can
observe a control, a system proves it.

5
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.372
People sign only for what no system
can see, like a policy approval

6
00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:21.188
or a physical inspection, and
the package says which is which.

7
00:00:21.188 --> 00:00:24.995
Day-two work feeds a loop:
map each control to its tests,

8
00:00:24.995 --> 00:00:30.013
test on a schedule, and turn every gap
into a tracked plan-of-action item.

9
00:00:30.013 --> 00:00:34.860
The decision for the system owner: close
those items only on a passing re-test,

10
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.862
and escalate a slipped milestone
instead of quietly moving it.

11
00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:40.560
Next, build or buy.
